    "description": {
      "en": "$PenAge ('Pension Age', latest 67) is the statutory state pension age (AOW-leeftijd), one of the most widely reused constants in the Dutch model, defined centrally in constdef_nl and consumed at 61 sites across the spine. It sets the household-age-group boundaries (A/C/E/G) for rent-allowance eligibility and calculation in bho_nl (literally 'dag<$PenAge' / 'dag>=$PenAge' per bho.md), is the qualifying age for the flat-rate state pension described in poa.md ('all residents who have reached the state pension age'), delimits the age-dependent net-to-gross conversion factors for social assistance in bsagross_nl/bsasegross_nl (Table 2.10 in bsagross.md), sets the #_AgeMin/#_AgeMax age bounds for social-assistance benefit rates in bsanet_nl/bsasenet_nl, and is referenced directly in tin_nl to determine eligibility for the old-age tax credit ('taxpayers aged above the state pension age ($PenAge)'). It is also used in bhlmt_nl (sickness benefit) and TransLMA_nl (labour-market transition eligibility)."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Pension age"
    },
